# Repo-wide: force LF for every file git detects as text, regardless of a
# given machine's core.autocrlf. Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (Git for
# Windows' default) re-materializes the whole working tree as CRLF on every
# fresh checkout -- confirmed live 2026-08-06: 207 files showed as "modified"
# after a plain `git checkout`/session restart on Windows, 100% whitespace
# noise (`git diff --stat -w` was empty), not real changes. The previous rule
# below only covered packaging scripts, so this same churn kept recurring on
# every other file in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Force LF line endings for Linux polkit packaging assets, regardless of the
# platform's core.autocrlf setting. These files are bundled verbatim into the
# .deb/.rpm packages and executed on Linux at package-install/runtime; a CRLF
# shebang (`#!/bin/sh\r`) breaks execution with "bad interpreter" errors.
# (Redundant with the repo-wide rule above now, kept for the specific
# rationale documented here.)
src-tauri/packaging/* text eol=lf
